// Ctrl+V: paste image from clipboard (if clipboard contains an image)
// Use Display.addFilter which fires BEFORE the native Text widget processes
// the keystroke — widget.addListener(KeyDown) fires too late on Windows
// where the native control has already consumed Ctrl+V for text paste.
Display.getDefault().addFilter(SWT.KeyDown, e -> {
    if (e.widget == inputField
            && (e.stateMask & SWT.MOD1) != 0
            && e.keyCode == 'v') {
        Clipboard cb = new Clipboard(Display.getDefault());
        try {
            if (cb.getContents(ImageTransfer.getInstance()) != null) {
                e.type = SWT.None; // suppress event completely
                if (attachmentManager != null) {
                    attachmentManager.pasteImage();
                }
            }
        } finally {
            cb.dispose();
        }
    }
});

