   - Eclipse plugin (SWT-based) for Claude Code CLI integration
   - SWT StyledText RTL handling: `setOrientation(SWT.RIGHT_TO_LEFT)` vs `setAlignment(SWT.RIGHT)` on Windows
   - Windows WS_EX_LAYOUTRTL coordinate mirroring causes double-mirror when both orientation and alignment are set
   - SWT native Text widget consumes Ctrl+V before Java KeyDown listeners fire
   - `Display.addFilter(SWT.KeyDown)` fires BEFORE widget-level processing
   - `inputField.addListener(SWT.KeyDown)` fires AFTER native widget processing
   - Eclipse plugin jar hot-patching via `jar uf` (update) vs `jar cf` (create - breaks plugin)
   - javac @argfile syntax to avoid Windows command line length limits
